    "updated_at": "2023-09-01T15:37:10Z",
    "body": "I agree that Telephone kind of \"sticks out funny\" and probably should not be an exception.\r\n\r\nI played with it [here](https://w3c.github.io/i18n-discuss/explainers/bidi-html-demo.html?text=%3Cinput%20type=button%20value=%22123%20456%22%3E%3Cbr%3E%0a%3Cinput%20type=button%20value=%22\\u0645\\u0635\\u0631!%22%20dir=auto%3E%3Cbr%3E%0a%3Cinput%20type=button%20value=%22\\u0645\\u0635\\u0631!%22%20dir=rtl%3E) a bit. \r\n\r\nI noticed a bug in FF: `dir=auto` doesn't work on the button's value (works in Chrome). My tendency is to think that the value should influence the button, but I'm not sure if there might be weird side effects.",
